# Team Context

Who works on this code determines how much context must be explicit. Solo developers rely on memory; large teams need everything written down.

## Options

TeamContexts {
  Solo => One person, everything in their head
  SmallTeam => 2-5 people, high bandwidth communication
  LargeTeam => 6+, async communication needed
  OpenSource => Unknown contributors, public scrutiny
  Handoff => Code will be given to others lacking context
}

## AI Behavior Calibration

BehaviorsByTeam {
  Solo => skip docs unless complex, follow existing style, optimize for author
  SmallTeam => brief "why" comments, follow patterns, mention things to discuss
  LargeTeam => doc public interfaces, enforce style, thorough reviews, consider onboarding
  OpenSource => comprehensive docs, strict style, explain commits, strong compat warnings
  Handoff => extensive docs, boring obvious solutions, document all decisions, avoid clever
}

## Documentation Matrix

| Context | Comments | README | Architecture | API Docs |
|---------|----------|--------|--------------|----------|
| Solo | Future-self | Setup | No | No |
| Small | Why not what | + context | Key decisions | Informal |
| Large | Public interfaces | Comprehensive | Yes | Yes |
| Open Source | Extensive | Contributor guide | Public | Full |
| Handoff | Everything | Complete | Thorough | Complete |

## Code Style

| Context | Enforcement | Cleverness | Abstractions |
|---------|-------------|------------|--------------|
| Solo | Personal | Fine | Preference |
| Small | Informal | Team understands | Discuss |
| Large | Automated | Avoid | Obvious |
| Open Source | Strict | Never | Documented |
| Handoff | Standard | Never | If documented |
